IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg8-nouns`
IMPORT `dg8-seat`

-- Worked cases for the seat layer dg8-seat.l4: the questions a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation asks of Subchapter IX, sections 263 to 268.
-- Every case states facts that person could state and an expected answer decided by reading the text of the section named (src:1277-1385) and written here before running; none was copied from the code's output.
-- At least one case for every question of the seat, and for most questions one case on each side of the answer.

§ `Worked cases`

-- My corporation and one other Delaware corporation want to merge with one partnership; no partnership law forbids it: section 263(a) lets them.
#ASSERT `May my corporation merge or consolidate with partnerships (s 263(a))` 2 1 FALSE
-- The partnership's own law forbids the merger: section 263(a) withholds the power.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation merge or consolidate with partnerships (s 263(a))` 1 1 TRUE)
-- No corporation of Delaware takes part, so the section gives no power.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation merge or consolidate with partnerships (s 263(a))` 0 1 FALSE)
-- My entity is described as in the definition of "partnership" in section 263(a).
#ASSERT `Is my entity a partnership within section 263 (s 263(a))` `entity that is a limited liability partnership`
-- An entity of that kind is not a "partnership" within the section.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my entity a partnership within section 263 (s 263(a))` `entity that is a limited liability company`)
-- A merger into a surviving Delaware corporation: terms, mode, certificate changes, manner of converting, what the other holders receive, and the other jurisdiction's requirements are all stated; the consolidation statement (4) is not required.
#ASSERT `Does our agreement of merger or consolidation state what section 263(b) requires (s 263(b))` `a merger into a surviving corporation of this State` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Some shares are cashed out and holders receive other consideration, but the agreement does not state what they receive: limb (5) fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does our agreement of merger or consolidation state what section 263(b) requires (s 263(b))` `a merger into a surviving corporation of this State` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- A consolidation into a new Delaware corporation whose agreement does not state that its certificate of incorporation is attached: limb (4) fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does our agreement of merger or consolidation state what section 263(b) requires (s 263(b))` `a consolidation into a new resulting corporation of this State` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- No written agreement has been entered into by each constituent.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does our agreement of merger or consolidation state what section 263(b) requires (s 263(b))` `a merger into a surviving corporation of this State` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- A term depends on an outside fact and the agreement clearly says how that fact operates.
#ASSERT `May a term of our agreement depend on facts outside the agreement (s 263(b))` TRUE TRUE
-- The agreement does not say how the outside fact operates on the term.
#ASSERT NOT (`May a term of our agreement depend on facts outside the agreement (s 263(b))` TRUE FALSE)
-- A cash-in-lieu arrangement for fractional shares that is consistent with section 155.
#ASSERT `May our agreement include this detail or provision (s 263(b)(6))` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- The fractional-share arrangement is not consistent with section 155.
#ASSERT NOT (`May our agreement include this detail or provision (s 263(b)(6))` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- I am a stockholder who will become a general partner of the surviving partnership: I must approve.
#ASSERT `Must I approve the merger or consolidation because I would become a general partner (s 263(c))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` TRUE
-- The survivor is a corporation, so no stockholder becomes a general partner of it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I approve the merger or consolidation because I would become a general partner (s 263(c))` `a merger into a surviving corporation of this State` TRUE)
-- The survivor is a partnership and a stockholder who will become a general partner has not approved.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has our agreement been approved as section 263(c) requires (s 263(c))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- The same stockholder has approved.
#ASSERT `Has our agreement been approved as section 263(c) requires (s 263(c))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- The survivor is a corporation: no extra approval is asked for.
#ASSERT `Has our agreement been approved as section 263(c) requires (s 263(c))` `a merger into a surviving corporation of this State` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- The agreement has been filed and takes effect on 1 July 2026; I ask about that day.
#ASSERT `Is the merger or consolidation in effect under the laws of Delaware (s 263(c))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1)
-- The day before it takes effect.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the merger or consolidation in effect under the laws of Delaware (s 263(c))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30))
-- A merger into a surviving Delaware corporation; the certificate states what (1) to (7) require and is executed under section 103.
#ASSERT `May we file a certificate of merger or consolidation instead of the agreement (s 263(c))` `a merger into a surviving corporation of this State` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- The certificate does not say that a copy of the agreement will be furnished free: (7) fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`May we file a certificate of merger or consolidation instead of the agreement (s 263(c))` `a merger into a surviving corporation of this State` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- A merger into a surviving partnership formed outside Delaware, executed by a general partner, and the certificate states the (d) agreement.
#ASSERT `May we file a certificate of merger or consolidation instead of the agreement (s 263(c))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- I am a stockholder of a constituent corporation and a certificate was filed in place of the agreement.
#ASSERT `Can I get a copy of the merger agreement on request and without cost (s 263(c)(7))` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- The agreement itself was filed, not a certificate: the statement that creates the claim was not required.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I get a copy of the merger agreement on request and without cost (s 263(c)(7))` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- I am neither a stockholder nor a partner of a constituent.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I get a copy of the merger agreement on request and without cost (s 263(c)(7))` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- The survivor is a partnership formed outside Delaware.
#ASSERT `Must the surviving partnership agree to be served with process in Delaware (s 263(d))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` TRUE
-- The partnership is formed in Delaware.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the surviving partnership agree to be served with process in Delaware (s 263(d))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` FALSE)
-- All four statements are made.
#ASSERT `Has the surviving partnership agreed to be served as section 263(d) requires (s 263(d))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- It has not specified an address for the Secretary of State to mail process to.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the surviving partnership agreed to be served as section 263(d) requires (s 263(d))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- I sue to enforce a constituent's obligation against a partnership formed outside Delaware.
#ASSERT `May I serve process on the Secretary of State to sue the surviving partnership (s 263(d))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` TRUE TRUE
-- My proceeding is not of the kinds the agreement covers.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I serve process on the Secretary of State to sue the surviving partnership (s 263(d))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` TRUE FALSE)
-- Electronic service as the Secretary of State prescribes.
#ASSERT `May I serve the Secretary of State by electronic transmission (s 263(d))` TRUE TRUE
-- Electronic service not as prescribed.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I serve the Secretary of State by electronic transmission (s 263(d))` TRUE FALSE)
-- Process has been served on the Secretary of State.
#ASSERT `Must the Secretary of State notify the surviving partnership by letter (s 263(d))` TRUE
-- No other address has been designated.
#ASSERT `To what address must the Secretary of State mail the letter (s 263(d))` "12 Quay Street" EMPTY EQUALS "12 Quay Street"
-- The last address designated in writing governs.
#ASSERT `To what address must the Secretary of State mail the letter (s 263(d))` "12 Quay Street" (LIST "9 Dock Road", "4 Mill Lane") EQUALS "4 Mill Lane"
-- Sent by courier with records, enclosing the process.
#ASSERT `Was the Secretary of State's letter sent as section 263(d) requires (s 263(d))` TRUE TRUE
-- The process was not enclosed.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was the Secretary of State's letter sent as section 263(d) requires (s 263(d))` TRUE FALSE)
-- I served in duplicate, notified the Secretary of State and paid the fee.
#ASSERT `Have I done what section 263(d) requires of a plaintiff (s 263(d))` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- I did not notify the Secretary of State.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I done what section 263(d) requires of a plaintiff (s 263(d))` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- If I prevail the fee is taxed as costs.
#ASSERT `Will the fee I pay the Secretary of State be taxed as costs (s 263(d))` TRUE
-- If I do not prevail it is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Will the fee I pay the Secretary of State be taxed as costs (s 263(d))` FALSE)
-- Received 15 January 2021: the fifth anniversary is still inside the five years.
#ASSERT `Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service (s 263(d))` (YearMonthDay 2021 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15)
-- The day after the fifth anniversary.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service (s 263(d))` (YearMonthDay 2021 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 16))
-- Sections 259 to 261 apply insofar as applicable.
#ASSERT `Does this provision apply to a merger between a corporation and a partnership (s 263(e))` `ss 259 to 261 as applied by s 263(e)` TRUE
-- Section 328 is not applicable to my merger.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does this provision apply to a merger between a corporation and a partnership (s 263(e))` `s 328 as applied by s 263(e)` FALSE)
-- My charitable corporation would merge into the partnership and lose its charitable status: the section does not authorize it.
#ASSERT `Does section 263 stop my charitable nonstock corporation merging into a partnership (s 263(f))` `a charitable nonstock corporation` TRUE TRUE
-- A stock corporation has no charitable status to lose.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 263 stop my charitable nonstock corporation merging into a partnership (s 263(f))` `a stock corporation` TRUE TRUE)
-- Its charitable status would not be lost or impaired.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 263 stop my charitable nonstock corporation merging into a partnership (s 263(f))` `a charitable nonstock corporation` TRUE FALSE)
-- A partnership may be merged into my charitable corporation, which survives.
#ASSERT `May a partnership be merged into my charitable nonstock corporation (s 263(f))` `a charitable nonstock corporation` TRUE
-- My corporation does not survive.
#ASSERT NOT (`May a partnership be merged into my charitable nonstock corporation (s 263(f))` `a charitable nonstock corporation` FALSE)
-- My corporation and one other Delaware corporation want to merge with one limited liability company; no limited liability company law forbids it: section 264(a) lets them.
#ASSERT `May my corporation merge or consolidate with limited liability companies (s 264(a))` 2 1 FALSE
-- The limited liability company's own law forbids the merger: section 264(a) withholds the power.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation merge or consolidate with limited liability companies (s 264(a))` 1 1 TRUE)
-- No corporation of Delaware takes part, so the section gives no power.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation merge or consolidate with limited liability companies (s 264(a))` 0 1 FALSE)
-- My entity is described as in the definition of "limited liability company" in section 264(a).
#ASSERT `Is my entity a limited liability company within section 264 (s 264(a))` `entity that is a limited liability company`
-- An entity of that kind is not a "limited liability company" within the section.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my entity a limited liability company within section 264 (s 264(a))` `entity that is a general partnership`)
-- A merger into a surviving Delaware corporation: terms, mode, certificate changes, manner of converting, what the other holders receive, and the other jurisdiction's requirements are all stated; the consolidation statement (4) is not required.
#ASSERT `Does our agreement of merger or consolidation state what section 264(b) requires (s 264(b))` `a merger into a surviving corporation of this State` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Some shares are cashed out and holders receive other consideration, but the agreement does not state what they receive: limb (5) fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does our agreement of merger or consolidation state what section 264(b) requires (s 264(b))` `a merger into a surviving corporation of this State` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- A consolidation into a new Delaware corporation whose agreement does not state that its certificate of incorporation is attached: limb (4) fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does our agreement of merger or consolidation state what section 264(b) requires (s 264(b))` `a consolidation into a new resulting corporation of this State` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- No written agreement has been entered into by each constituent.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does our agreement of merger or consolidation state what section 264(b) requires (s 264(b))` `a merger into a surviving corporation of this State` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- A term depends on an outside fact and the agreement clearly says how that fact operates.
#ASSERT `May a term of our agreement depend on facts outside the agreement (s 264(b))` TRUE TRUE
-- The agreement does not say how the outside fact operates on the term.
#ASSERT NOT (`May a term of our agreement depend on facts outside the agreement (s 264(b))` TRUE FALSE)
-- A cash-in-lieu arrangement for fractional shares that is consistent with section 155.
#ASSERT `May our agreement include this detail or provision (s 264(b)(6))` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- The fractional-share arrangement is not consistent with section 155.
#ASSERT NOT (`May our agreement include this detail or provision (s 264(b)(6))` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Each corporation and each limited liability company has approved as the subsection requires.
#ASSERT `Has our agreement been approved as section 264(c) requires (s 264(c))` TRUE TRUE
-- A limited liability company has not approved under its limited liability company agreement.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has our agreement been approved as section 264(c) requires (s 264(c))` TRUE FALSE)
-- The agreement has been filed and takes effect on 1 July 2026; I ask about that day.
#ASSERT `Is the merger or consolidation in effect under the laws of Delaware (s 264(c))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1)
-- The day before it takes effect.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the merger or consolidation in effect under the laws of Delaware (s 264(c))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30))
-- A merger into a surviving Delaware corporation; the certificate states what (1) to (7) require and is executed under section 103.
#ASSERT `May we file a certificate of merger or consolidation instead of the agreement (s 264(c))` `a merger into a surviving corporation of this State` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- The certificate does not say that a copy of the agreement will be furnished free: (7) fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`May we file a certificate of merger or consolidation instead of the agreement (s 264(c))` `a merger into a surviving corporation of this State` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- A merger into a surviving limited liability company formed outside Delaware, executed by an authorized person, and the certificate states the (d) agreement.
#ASSERT `May we file a certificate of merger or consolidation instead of the agreement (s 264(c))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- I am a stockholder of a constituent corporation and a certificate was filed in place of the agreement.
#ASSERT `Can I get a copy of the merger agreement on request and without cost (s 264(c)(7))` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- The agreement itself was filed, not a certificate: the statement that creates the claim was not required.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I get a copy of the merger agreement on request and without cost (s 264(c)(7))` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- I am neither a stockholder nor a member of a constituent.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I get a copy of the merger agreement on request and without cost (s 264(c)(7))` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- The survivor is a limited liability company formed outside Delaware.
#ASSERT `Must the surviving limited liability company agree to be served with process in Delaware (s 264(d))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` TRUE
-- The limited liability company is formed in Delaware.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the surviving limited liability company agree to be served with process in Delaware (s 264(d))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` FALSE)
-- All four statements are made.
#ASSERT `Has the surviving limited liability company agreed to be served as section 264(d) requires (s 264(d))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- It has not specified an address for the Secretary of State to mail process to.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the surviving limited liability company agreed to be served as section 264(d) requires (s 264(d))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- I sue to enforce a constituent's obligation against a limited liability company formed outside Delaware.
#ASSERT `May I serve process on the Secretary of State to sue the surviving limited liability company (s 264(d))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` TRUE TRUE
-- My proceeding is not of the kinds the agreement covers.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I serve process on the Secretary of State to sue the surviving limited liability company (s 264(d))` `a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation` TRUE FALSE)
-- Electronic service as the Secretary of State prescribes.
#ASSERT `May I serve the Secretary of State by electronic transmission (s 264(d))` TRUE TRUE
-- Electronic service not as prescribed.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I serve the Secretary of State by electronic transmission (s 264(d))` TRUE FALSE)
-- Process has been served on the Secretary of State.
#ASSERT `Must the Secretary of State notify the surviving limited liability company by letter (s 264(d))` TRUE
-- No other address has been designated.
#ASSERT `To what address must the Secretary of State mail the letter (s 264(d))` "12 Quay Street" EMPTY EQUALS "12 Quay Street"
-- The last address designated in writing governs.
#ASSERT `To what address must the Secretary of State mail the letter (s 264(d))` "12 Quay Street" (LIST "9 Dock Road", "4 Mill Lane") EQUALS "4 Mill Lane"
-- Sent by courier with records, enclosing the process.
#ASSERT `Was the Secretary of State's letter sent as section 264(d) requires (s 264(d))` TRUE TRUE
-- The process was not enclosed.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was the Secretary of State's letter sent as section 264(d) requires (s 264(d))` TRUE FALSE)
-- I served in duplicate, notified the Secretary of State and paid the fee.
#ASSERT `Have I done what section 264(d) requires of a plaintiff (s 264(d))` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- I did not notify the Secretary of State.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I done what section 264(d) requires of a plaintiff (s 264(d))` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- If I prevail the fee is taxed as costs.
#ASSERT `Will the fee I pay the Secretary of State be taxed as costs (s 264(d))` TRUE
-- If I do not prevail it is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Will the fee I pay the Secretary of State be taxed as costs (s 264(d))` FALSE)
-- Received 15 January 2021: the fifth anniversary is still inside the five years.
#ASSERT `Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service (s 264(d))` (YearMonthDay 2021 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15)
-- The day after the fifth anniversary.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service (s 264(d))` (YearMonthDay 2021 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 16))
-- Sections 259 to 261 apply insofar as applicable.
#ASSERT `Does this provision apply to a merger between a corporation and a limited liability company (s 264(e))` `ss 259 to 261 as applied by s 264(e)` TRUE
-- Section 328 is not applicable to my merger.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does this provision apply to a merger between a corporation and a limited liability company (s 264(e))` `s 328 as applied by s 264(e)` FALSE)
-- My charitable corporation would merge into the limited liability company and lose its charitable status: the section does not authorize it.
#ASSERT `Does section 264 stop my charitable nonstock corporation merging into a limited liability company (s 264(f))` `a charitable nonstock corporation` TRUE TRUE
-- A stock corporation has no charitable status to lose.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 264 stop my charitable nonstock corporation merging into a limited liability company (s 264(f))` `a stock corporation` TRUE TRUE)
-- Its charitable status would not be lost or impaired.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 264 stop my charitable nonstock corporation merging into a limited liability company (s 264(f))` `a charitable nonstock corporation` TRUE FALSE)
-- A limited liability company may be merged into my charitable corporation, which survives.
#ASSERT `May a limited liability company be merged into my charitable nonstock corporation (s 264(f))` `a charitable nonstock corporation` TRUE
-- My corporation does not survive.
#ASSERT NOT (`May a limited liability company be merged into my charitable nonstock corporation (s 264(f))` `a charitable nonstock corporation` FALSE)
-- A statutory trust is an "other entity".
#ASSERT `Is my entity an other entity that may convert to a corporation of this State (s 265(a))` `entity that is a statutory trust`
-- A corporation of this State is not an "other entity".
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my entity an other entity that may convert to a corporation of this State (s 265(a))` `entity that is a corporation formed under the laws of Delaware`)
-- A foreign corporation is an "other entity".
#ASSERT `Is my entity an other entity that may convert to a corporation of this State (s 265(a))` `entity that is a corporation formed under the laws of a foreign country`
-- A natural person is not an entity.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my entity an other entity that may convert to a corporation of this State (s 265(a))` `entity that is a natural person`)
-- Our LLC filed both certificates simultaneously with the same effective date.
#ASSERT `Have we converted to a corporation of this State by filing as section 265(b) requires (s 265(b))` `entity that is a limited liability company` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Not effective upon filing and no same effective date provided.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have we converted to a corporation of this State by filing as section 265(b) requires (s 265(b))` `entity that is a limited liability company` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- The certificates were not filed simultaneously.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have we converted to a corporation of this State by filing as section 265(b) requires (s 265(b))` `entity that is a limited liability company` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Our jurisdiction has changed and the certificate says so; no plan of conversion is adopted.
#ASSERT `Does our certificate of conversion state what section 265(c) requires (s 265(c))` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- The jurisdiction has changed but the certificate does not state the jurisdiction immediately before conversion.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does our certificate of conversion state what section 265(c) requires (s 265(c))` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- A plan of conversion is adopted but the certificate does not say its provisions will be approved first.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does our certificate of conversion state what section 265(c) requires (s 265(c))` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Effective 1 September 2026; asking about that day.
#ASSERT `Has my entity become a corporation of this State on the day I am asking about (s 265(d))` (YearMonthDay 2026 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 9 1)
-- The day before.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my entity become a corporation of this State on the day I am asking about (s 265(d))` (YearMonthDay 2026 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 8 31))
-- Notwithstanding section 106, the existence dates from when the LLC first came into being.
#ASSERT `When is the existence of my corporation deemed to have begun (s 265(d))` (YearMonthDay 2003 11 20) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2003 11 20
-- A liability I incurred before the conversion.
#ASSERT `Does the conversion leave my earlier liability untouched (s 265(e))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A liability incurred after: section 265(e) says nothing.
#ASSERT `Does the conversion leave my earlier liability untouched (s 265(e))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Once effective, six consequences follow.
#ASSERT count (`What follows once my entity has converted to a corporation of this State (s 265(f))` TRUE) EQUALS 6
-- Before it is effective, none.
#ASSERT null (`What follows once my entity has converted to a corporation of this State (s 265(f))` FALSE)
-- Effective: debts remain attached to the corporation.
#ASSERT `Do the converted entity's debts remain enforceable against the corporation (s 265(f))` TRUE
-- Not yet effective.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the converted entity's debts remain enforceable against the corporation (s 265(f))` FALSE)
-- Nothing agreed otherwise and no non-Delaware law requires winding up.
#ASSERT `Is my converting entity spared winding up (s 265(g))` FALSE FALSE
-- We agreed otherwise.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my converting entity spared winding up (s 265(g))` TRUE FALSE)
-- No agreement and no non-Delaware requirement.
#ASSERT `Is the conversion a continuation and not a dissolution (s 265(g))` FALSE FALSE
-- Non-Delaware law requires otherwise.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the conversion a continuation and not a dissolution (s 265(g))` FALSE TRUE)
-- Approved in the manner our writing provides, before the certificate took effect, with the same authorization for the certificate of incorporation.
#ASSERT `Has the conversion been approved as section 265(h) requires (s 265(h))` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Approval came after the certificate took effect.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the conversion been approved as section 265(h) requires (s 265(h))` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Signed by an authorized person.
#ASSERT `Is the certificate of conversion signed as section 265(i) requires (s 265(i))` TRUE
-- Signed by someone unauthorized.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the certificate of conversion signed as section 265(i) requires (s 265(i))` FALSE)
-- Cancelling interests is allowed.
#ASSERT `May the interests in my entity be exchanged, converted or cancelled this way (s 265(j))` `cancelled` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A treatment the subsection does not list is not covered.
#ASSERT `May the interests in my entity be exchanged, converted or cancelled this way (s 265(j))` `any treatment that subsection (j) does not list` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The plan may state its terms and conditions.
#ASSERT `May our plan of conversion state this matter (s 265(k))` `the terms and conditions of the conversion under s 265(k)(i)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A matter outside the six listed is not covered.
#ASSERT `May our plan of conversion state this matter (s 265(k))` `any matter that subsection (k) does not list` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Stated in the plan and approved under the law applicable to the other entity.
#ASSERT `Has the corporate action stated in our plan been approved as section 265(k)(iv) requires (s 265(k)(iv))` TRUE TRUE
-- Stated but not so approved.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the corporate action stated in our plan been approved as section 265(k)(iv) requires (s 265(k)(iv))` TRUE FALSE)
-- The plan sets out how the outside fact operates.
#ASSERT `May a term of our plan of conversion depend on facts outside the plan (s 265(k))` TRUE TRUE
-- It does not.
#ASSERT NOT (`May a term of our plan of conversion depend on facts outside the plan (s 265(k))` TRUE FALSE)
-- Set forth in an approved plan and within Subchapter II powers: as director I need take no further action.
#ASSERT `Does a corporate action in our plan need no further action by the board, stockholders or members (s 265(l))` TRUE TRUE
-- It is outside the powers of a corporation.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does a corporate action in our plan need no further action by the board, stockholders or members (s 265(l))` TRUE FALSE)
-- The certificate states that no further action is required.
#ASSERT `Is the certificate we file under another section as section 265(l) requires (s 265(l))` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- The certificate omits the statement.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the certificate we file under another section as section 265(l) requires (s 265(l))` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- To a limited liability company, once authorized.
#ASSERT `May my corporation convert to this entity (s 266(a))` `entity that is a limited liability company` TRUE
-- Not to a corporation of this State.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation convert to this entity (s 266(a))` `entity that is a corporation formed under the laws of Delaware` TRUE)
-- Not yet authorized in accordance with the section.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation convert to this entity (s 266(a))` `entity that is a limited liability company` FALSE)
-- Resolution adopted, specifying the entity and recommending approval; no plan.
#ASSERT `Has the board adopted the resolution section 266(b) requires (s 266(b))` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- A plan is to be adopted but was not approved together with the resolution.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the board adopted the resolution section 266(b) requires (s 266(b))` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- I hold nonvoting stock: I am still entitled to notice.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to notice of the meeting on the conversion (s 266(b))` TRUE
-- I hold no stock.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to notice of the meeting on the conversion (s 266(b))` FALSE)
-- Notice given on the 20th day before the meeting.
#ASSERT `Was notice of the meeting given to me as section 266(b) requires (s 266(b))` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)
-- Notice given 19 days before.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was notice of the meeting given to me as section 266(b) requires (s 266(b))` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 11) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30))
-- Submitted at a special meeting where a vote was taken.
#ASSERT `Was the resolution put to the stockholders as section 266(b) requires (s 266(b))` TRUE TRUE
-- No vote was taken.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was the resolution put to the stockholders as section 266(b) requires (s 266(b))` TRUE FALSE)
-- 51 votes of 100 is a majority.
#ASSERT `Does the stockholders' vote carry the resolution (s 266(b))` 51 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Half is not a majority.
#ASSERT `Does the stockholders' vote carry the resolution (s 266(b))` 50 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- More votes than there are: not a vote the Law covers.
#ASSERT `Does the stockholders' vote carry the resolution (s 266(b))` 101 100 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Converting to a partnership with general partners and I will become one.
#ASSERT `Must I approve the conversion because I would become a general partner (s 266(b))` TRUE TRUE
-- I will not become one.
